# Adding a package whose types form an exponential value-containment fan-out must
# fail cleanly at type-check time, NOT hang the node. go/types' validType walk is
# exponential on such types and runs unmetered at addpkg, so the deploy path prices
# the walk and charges for it BEFORE handing the package to go/types.
#
# This chain's walk is ~2^41 nodes, which no legal gas budget covers (a whole block
# is 3e9 gas), so the charge aborts the deploy on gas. Nothing rejects it for being
# "too complex" — it is refused for being unaffordable, and the same shape would
# deploy if it were small enough for the sender to pay for.
#
# Measured against master, this archive wedges the node rather than failing: the
# node never answers, and after 60s gnokey gives up with
#
#   unable to call RPC method abci_query ... context deadline exceeded
#   broadcast.go:245 - simulate tx
#
# Note where that lands — abci_query during SIMULATE, a read-only path with no fee
# and no tx inclusion. Here the same input returns out of gas in ~2s.

# start a new node
gnoland start

# the fan-out package cannot pay for the walk it would cause
! gnokey maketx addpkg -pkgdir $WORK/fanout -pkgpath gno.land/r/foobar/fanout -gas-fee 350001ugnot -gas-wanted 20_000_000 -chainid=tendermint_test $test1_user_addr
stderr 'out of gas'

-- fanout/gnomod.toml --
module = "gno.land/r/foobar/fanout"
gno = "0.9"

-- fanout/fanout.gno --
package fanout

type T0 struct{ v int }
type T1 struct{ a, b [0]T0 }
type T2 struct{ a, b [0]T1 }
